  "query_preview": "..\n(Wednesday night through Monday)\nIssued at 147 AM CST Tue Nov 17 2026\n\nWinds Tuesday evening are likely to remain in the 15 to 25 mph \nrange, hindering some fog development, but areas with light winds \ncould still see reductions in visibilities due to continued high \nrelative humidity. As mid to upper level ridging remain in place, a \nslight warming trend is expected through the remainder of the work \nweek with high tempertures forecast to be in the low to mid 70s and \nlows in the low to mid 50s by Thursday and Friday. Upper level \ntroughing, currently located over the Pacific SW, will approach the \narea late Friday into early Saturday, followed by a cold front early \nSunday morning, bringing a cooling trend to the region. A secondary \nshortwave upper level trough is expected to progress across the \nregion early next week, increasing rain chances across the region.\n\nBynum",
